<metadata_system id="176" name="Scanner Metadata" category="IMG" category_label="Images" used_for="Document/photo scanner output (TWAIN/WIA/ISIS-driven)" spec_source="TWAIN 2.4 Specification + Microsoft WIA + Pixel Translations ISIS" completeness="comprehensive" record_count="66">
  <description>Scanner metadata divides into three layers: (1) TWAIN/WIA/ISIS driver capabilities — what the scanner reports it can do (resolution, color modes, ADF status, paper sizes, duplex, batch settings, blank-page detection); (2) per-scan settings actually applied (chosen DPI, bit depth, region, brightness/contrast, output format); (3) embedded metadata in the output file (EXIF Make/Model/Software/DateTime, XMP CreatorTool, PDF Producer/Creator). TWAIN is the cross-platform standard used by most consumer scanners; WIA is Microsoft's Windows-native alternative; ISIS is the high-end production-scanner standard from EMC Captiva. This entry covers the comprehensive capability and image-info catalogs from all three.</description>
